 is extremely large, the calculation `flashloanVars.destAmount - (flashloanVars.destAmount / 1000)` results in an integer overflow when calculating the amount to be repaid or supplied. || This overflowed amount is then used in subsequent Aave V3 operations (borrow/supply) within `repayAllDebtAssetsWithFlashLoan` and `repayFlashloansAndTransferToTreasury`. || The overflowed amount leads to an excessive amount of WETH being credited to the attacker's address, effectively draining the protocol's WETH reserves. || Finally, the attacker repays the flash loan and transfers the stolen WETH to their own address.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "1 verified, 0 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.75, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploited an integer overflow vulnerability in the `ConnectorDeleverageParaswap` contract's `flashloanReq` function. This function is designed to handle flash loans and subsequent swaps. The vulnerability arises from how the `swapData` parameter is processed. Specifically, when constructing the `FlashloanVars` struct within the `deloopAllCollaterals` function, the `_getParaswapData` helper function decodes `swapData`. The `destAmount` from this decoding is used to calculate `debtAmounts`. If `destAmount` is extremely large, the subtraction `flashloanVars.destAmount - (flashloanVars.destAmount / 1000)` can result in a value that, when used in subsequent Aave V3 `borrow` or `supply` operations within the `repayAllDebtAssetsWithFlashLoan` and `repayFlashloansAndTransferToTreasury` functions, causes an integer overflow. This overflow leads to an incorrect calculation of the amount of WETH the attacker receives, allowing them to drain a disproportionately large amount of WETH from the protocol. The attack involves initiating a flash loan, performing a series of swaps via ParaSwap (as indicated by the `swapData`), and then using the overflowed amounts to repay debts and withdraw excessive collateral.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "Integer Overflow", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Integer Overflow", "attack_title": "Contract : https://etherscan.io/address/0x11a8dc866c5d03ff06bb74565b6575537b215978", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x9f54e8eaa9658316bb8006e03fff1cb191aafbe6", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2024_07_doughfina/contracts/01_vulnerable_9f54e8ea_connectordeleverageparaswap", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.24+commit.e11b9ed9", "contract_name": "ConnectorDeleverageParaswap", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x9f54e8eaa9658316bb8006e03fff1cb191aafbe6", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:25:11.121Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2024_07_doughfina/contracts/01_vulnerable_9f54e8ea_connectordeleverageparaswap/sources/@aave/core-v3/contracts/flashloan/base/FlashLoanReceiverBase.sol", "data/contracts/2024_07_doughfina/contracts/01_vulnerable_9f54e8ea_connectordeleverageparaswap/sources/@aave/core-v3/contracts/flashloan/interfaces/IFlashLoanReceiver.sol", "data/contracts/2024_07_doughfina/contracts/01_vulnerable_9f54e8ea_connectordeleverageparaswap/sources/@aave/core-v3/contracts/interfaces/IPool.sol", "data/contracts/2024_07_doughfina/contracts/01_vulnerable_9f54e8ea_connectordeleverageparaswap/sources/@aave/core-v3/contracts/interfaces/IPoolAddressesProvider.sol", "data/contracts/2024_07_doughfina/contracts/01_vulnerable_9f54e8ea_connectordeleverageparaswap/sources/@aave/core-v3/contracts/interfaces/IPoolDataProvider.sol", "data/contracts/2024_07_doughfina/contracts/01_vulnerable_9f54e8ea_connectordeleverageparaswap/sources/@aave/core-v3/contracts/protocol/libraries/types/DataTypes.sol", 