ol. The attacker then used SushiSwap to convert the stolen assets into ETH.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `IPool` contract's `deposit` and `withdraw` functions lack sufficient checks or have flawed logic in calculating the relationship between deposited amounts, internal balances, and liquidity tokens. This allows an attacker to manipulate the pool's state to their advantage.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy", "attack_title": "Tx : https://arbiscan.io/tx/0x57c96e320a3b885fabd95dd476d43c0d0fb10500d940d9594d4a458471a87abe", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x15a024061c151045ba483e9243291dee6ee5fd8a", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_10_belugadex/contracts/01_vulnerable_15a02406_adminupgradeabilityproxy", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 42161, "name": "Arbitrum One"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.9+commit.e5eed63a", "contract_name": "AdminUpgradeabilityProxy", "explorer_url": "https://arbiscan.io/address/0x15a024061c151045ba483e9243291dee6ee5fd8a", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0xa403ed95cf10efeffa8128b47b6da8d5e6a27261", "is_proxy": true, "proxy_type": "EIP1967", "resolution_depth": 1, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:25:41.984Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_10_belugadex/contracts/01_vulnerable_15a02406_adminupgradeabilityproxy/sources/Users/build/.repo/evm-contract-jerry.git/bela/contracts/proxy/AdminUpgradeabilityProxy.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The BelugaDex protocol's `IPool` contract is vulnerable to a flash loan attack. The attacker exploited a flaw in how the `deposit` and `withdraw` functions interact with liquidity pools, allowing them to manipulate token balances and extract funds. Specifically, the attacker used a series of flash loans and strategic swaps to drain liquidity from the pools.", "verification_status": "proxy"}, {"abi_available": true, "address": "0xa403ed95cf