t properly validate the signatures provided by the users. Specifically, the `_validate` function, which is responsible for verifying signatures, iterates through the provided `v`, `r`, and `s` arrays and uses `ecrecover` to recover the signer's address. It then checks if the recovered address is an owner of the multisig wallet. However, it does not check if the same owner has already signed the transaction or if the signatures are unique. This allows an attacker to reuse or forge signatures from existing owners to authorize arbitrary withdrawals. In this specific attack, the attacker provided forged signatures to withdraw a significant amount of WBTC from the bridge.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "Signature Replay/Forging", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Signature Replay/Forging", "attack_title": "Tx (WBTC) : https://explorer.phalcon.xyz/tx/eth/0xe0bada18fdc56dec125c31b1636490f85ba66016318060a066ed7050ff7271f9", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x1bf68a9d1eaee7826b3593c20a0ca93293cb489a", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2024_01_orbitchain/contracts/01_vulnerable_1bf68a9d_ethvault", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.5.0+commit.1d4f565a", "contract_name": "EthVault", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x1bf68a9d1eaee7826b3593c20a0ca93293cb489a", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0xc3430bc8c2c05fc6b42114bf7f82a3e2f3ee9454", "is_proxy": true, "proxy_type": "EIP1967", "resolution_depth": 1, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:28:02.558Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2024_01_orbitchain/contracts/01_vulnerable_1bf68a9d_ethvault/sources/EthVault.impl.sol", "data/contracts/2024_01_orbitchain/contracts/01_vulnerable_1bf68a9d_ethvault/sources/EthVault.sol", "data/contracts/2024_01_orbitchain/contracts/01_vulnerable_1bf68a9d_ethvault/sources/MultiSigWallet.sol", "data/contra