{"ai_attack_steps": ["The attacker deploys a `Mock` contract that implements the `ICvxStakingPositionService` interface.", "The `claimCvgCvxMultiple` function in the `Mock` contract is designed to return an extremely large value for the claimed CVG tokens (`type(uint256).max - CVG.totalSupply()`).", "The attacker then calls `claimMultipleStaking` on the `ICvxRewardDistributor` contract.", "The attacker passes the `Mock` contract as one of the `claimContracts`, sets `_minCvgCvxAmountOut` to 1, and `_isConvert` to true.", "The `claimMultipleStaking` function iterates through the provided `claimContracts`. When it calls `claimCvgCvxMultiple` on the `Mock` contract, it receives the excessively large CVG amount.", "Without proper validation of the returned CVG amount, the contract proceeds to the conversion logic (due to `_isConvert` being true). This conversion, involving the massive CVG amount, leads to an integer overflow/underflow.", "The overflow/underflow results in the attacker receiving a disproportionately large amount of CVG tokens, effectively minting them."], "ai_attack_steps_text": "The attacker deploys a `Mock` contract that implements the `ICvxStakingPositionService` interface. || The `claimCvgCvxMultiple` function in the `Mock` contract is designed to return an extremely large value for the claimed CVG tokens (`type(uint256).max - CVG.totalSupply()`). || The attacker then calls `claimMultipleStaking` on the `ICvxRewardDistributor` contract. || The attacker passes the `Mock` contract as one of the `claimContracts`, sets `_minCvgCvxAmountOut` to 1, and `_isConvert` to true. || The `claimMultipleStaking` function iterates through the provided `claimContracts`. When it calls `claimCvgCvxMultiple` on the `Mock` contract, it receives the excessively large CVG amount. || Without proper validation of the returned CVG amount, the contract proceeds to the conversion logic (due to `_isConvert` being true). This conversion, involving the massive CVG amount, leads to an integer overflow/underflow. || The overflow/underflow results in the attacker receiving a disproportionately large amount of CVG tokens, effectively minting them.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "2 verified, 1 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.95, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The vulnerability lies in the `claimMultipleStaking` function of the `CvxRewardDistributorV2` contract. This function iterates through a list of `claimContracts` and calls their `claimCvgCvxMultiple` function. The `claimCvgCvxMultiple` function in the `Mock` contract, deployed by the attacker, returns an extremely large value (`type(uint256).max - CVG.totalSupply()`) for the claimed CVG tokens. The `claimMultipleStaking` function does not properly validate this returned amount. When `_isConvert` is true, the contract attempts to convert these CVG tokens (potentially through a DEX like Curve) using the provided `_minCvgCvxAmountOut` and `cvxRewardCount` parameters. Due to the massive, unvalidated amount returned by the mock contract, this conversion process results in an integer overflow/underflow, allowing the attacker to mint an excessive amount of CVG tokens.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "Integer Overflow/Underflow", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Integer Overflow/Underflow", "attack_title": "Convergence_exp", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x2b083beaac310cc5e190b1d2507038ccb03e7606", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2024_08_convergence/contracts/01_vulnerable_2b083bea_transparentupgradeableproxy", "bytecode_available": false, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.24+commit.e11b9ed9", "contract_name": "TransparentUpgradeableProxy", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x2b083beaac310cc5e190b1d2507038ccb03e7606", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0x394f61d