{"ai_attack_steps": ["The attacker first borrowed crETH and crAMP from Cream Finance.", "The attacker then initiated a swap on Uniswap V2 using the borrowed crETH and crAMP.", "The Uniswap V2 swap triggered the `uniswapV2Call` hook in the attacker's contract.", "Inside `uniswapV2Call`, the attacker called `creth.mint()`, which re-entered the `CEther.mint` function.", "The reentrant call to `CEther.mint` allowed the attacker to borrow an additional amount of crETH.", "The `tokensReceived` function was also triggered, leading to another borrow of crETH.", "Finally, the attacker transferred the stolen WETH to their own wallet.", "The attacker also transferred WETH to a Uniswap V2 pair."], "ai_attack_steps_text": "The attacker first borrowed crETH and crAMP from Cream Finance. || The attacker then initiated a swap on Uniswap V2 using the borrowed crETH and crAMP. || The Uniswap V2 swap triggered the `uniswapV2Call` hook in the attacker's contract. || Inside `uniswapV2Call`, the attacker called `creth.mint()`, which re-entered the `CEther.mint` function. || The reentrant call to `CEther.mint` allowed the attacker to borrow an additional amount of crETH. || The `tokensReceived` function was also triggered, leading to another borrow of crETH. || Finally, the attacker transferred the stolen WETH to their own wallet. || The attacker also transferred WETH to a Uniswap V2 pair.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "3 verified, 1 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 1.0, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploited a reentrancy vulnerability in the `CEther.mint` function, which is called via the `uniswapV2Call` hook. The `uniswapV2Call` function is triggered when a user interacts with a Uniswap V2 pair. In this exploit, the attacker first borrowed crETH and crAMP, then used these borrowed assets to perform a swap on Uniswap V2. This swap triggered the `uniswapV2Call` function. Inside `uniswapV2Call`, the attacker called `creth.mint()`, which re-entered the `CEther.mint` function before the initial call had finished. This reentrancy allowed the attacker to borrow more crETH than they should have been able to, effectively draining the protocol's funds. The `tokensReceived` function was also called, leading to another borrow of crETH. Finally, the attacker transferred WETH to a Uniswap V2 pair and their own wallet.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The root cause of the exploit is a reentrancy vulnerability in the `CEther.mint` function. The `mint` function does not properly check for reentrancy before performing critical state changes. This allows an attacker to call the `mint` function multiple times within a single transaction, leading to an excessive amount of assets being borrowed. The interaction with Uniswap V2's `uniswapV2Call` hook and the `tokensReceived` function provided the mechanism for the reentrant calls.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy", "attack_title": "Cream_exp", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0xd06527d5e56a3495252a528c4987003b712860ee", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2021_08_cream/contracts/01_vulnerable_d06527d5_cether", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.5.17+commit.d19bba13", "contract_name": "CEther", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0xd06527d5e56a3495252a528c4987003b712860ee", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:32:36.617Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2021_08_cream/contracts/01_vulnerable_d06527d5_cether/sources/contracts/CEther.sol", "data/contracts/2021_08_cream/contracts/01_vulnerable_d06527d5_cether/sources/contracts/CToken.sol", "data/contracts/2021_08_cream/contracts/01_vulnerable_d06527d5