 0.85, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploited the `VLFI` contract by creating a series of `Claimer` contracts. The `stake` function in `VLFI` allowed staking on behalf of another address. The `Claimer` contract's `delegate` function called `VLFI.claimRewards` and then deployed a new `Claimer` contract, transferring a portion of VLFI to it. This created an unbounded loop where rewards could be claimed and transferred indefinitely, draining the `VLFI` contract. The `claimRewards` function itself did not have reentrancy guards, and the attacker leveraged the ability to create new contracts within the reward claiming process to bypass any potential checks and continuously claim rewards.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "Reentrancy vulnerability combined with an unbounded loop of contract creation and reward claiming. The `claimRewards` function in the `VLFI` contract did not implement proper reentrancy guards. The attacker exploited this by creating new `Claimer` contracts within the `claimRewards` function's execution flow, allowing them to repeatedly call `claimRewards` before the initial call could complete, effectively draining the contract.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy", "attack_title": "Tx : https://polygonscan.com/tx/0x051f80a7ef69e1ffad889ec7e1f7d29a9e80883156b5c8528438b5bb8b7a689a", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0xfc604b6fd73a1bc60d31be111f798dd0d4137812", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_05_lfi/contracts/01_vulnerable_fc604b6f_transparentupgradeableproxy", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 137, "name": "Polygon"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.2+commit.661d1103", "contract_name": "TransparentUpgradeableProxy", "explorer_url": "https://polygonscan.com/address/0xfc604b6fd73a1bc60d31be111f798dd0d4137812", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0xd346309df75eb6832bdc90dd8ba3b8e0264c97e3", "is_proxy": true, "prox