ack involved repeatedly calling the `deliver` function. By manipulating the token balances and reflections, the attacker was able to mint a large amount of HODL tokens. These newly minted tokens were then swapped for WETH on the HODL-WETH Uniswap pair, effectively draining the liquidity and profiting the attacker. The attacker also utilized the `isExcludedFromFee` and `isExcluded` functions to bypass certain fee mechanisms within the HODL token, further enhancing their ability to exploit the contract.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `deliver` function in the HODLCapital token contract lacks proper validation. It allows for excessive token minting when combined with other operations, such as swaps on the Uniswap pair, by not adequately checking the sender's status (e.g., if they are excluded from fees) or the contract's state (e.g., if a swap is in progress). This leads to an uncontrolled inflation of the token supply, benefiting the attacker at the expense of other token holders and liquidity providers.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Token Inflation", "attack_title": "er Transaction : https://etherscan.io/tx/0xedc214a62ff6fd764200ddaa8ceae54f842279eadab80900be5f29d0b75212df", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0xeda47e13fd1192e32226753dc2261c4a14908fb7", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_05_hodlcapital/contracts/01_vulnerable_eda47e13_hodlcapital", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.6.12+commit.27d51765", "contract_name": "HODLCapital", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0xeda47e13fd1192e32226753dc2261c4a14908fb7", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:34:35.351Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_05_hodlcapital/contracts/01_vulnerable_eda47e13_hodlcapital/source.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The HODL token contract has a vulnerability that allows an attacker to drain funds. The `deliver` function, when called with a large amount, can lead to an inflation of the token supply. The attacker exploits this by repeatedly calling `deliver` and then swapping tokens on a Uniswap pair, effectively minting tokens and transferring them to their own address.", "verification_status": "verified"}], "contracts_dir": "data/contracts/2023_05_hodlcapital", "id": "2023_05_hodlcapital", "metadata": {"ai_enabled": true, "ai_model": "gemini-2.5-flash-lite|gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "dataset_version": "1.0.0", "poc_parser_version": "1.0.0", "processed_at": "2026-04-10T06:34:38.708Z"}, "num_bytecode_contracts": 1, "num_contracts": 1, "num_source_contracts": 1, "num_verified_contracts": 1, "poc_code": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED
