{"ai_attack_steps": ["The attacker deploys a malicious contract that implements the `onERC721Received` function.", "The attacker calls the `Stake` function on the `SMOOFSStaking` contract, transferring their Smoofs NFT and paying the `nftStakeCarryAmount` in MOOVE tokens.", "The `Stake` function internally calls `nftCollection.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), _tokenId)`, which triggers the `onERC721Received` function in the attacker's contract.", "Inside the attacker's `onERC721Received` function, a loop is initiated. This loop repeatedly calls the `SMOOFSStaking.Withdraw(_tokenId, true)` function.", "The `Withdraw` function, when `forceWithTax` is true, bypasses the tax logic and allows for repeated reward claims and NFT withdrawals without proper state checks or tax application.", "The loop continues until a predefined condition is met (e.g., a certain number of iterations or until the contract's balance is depleted), draining the rewards and potentially the principal from the `SMOOFSStaking` contract.", "Finally, the attacker's contract withdraws the NFT and any remaining MOOVE tokens.", "The attacker's contract then transfers the drained MOOVE tokens to their own address."], "ai_attack_steps_text": "The attacker deploys a malicious contract that implements the `onERC721Received` function. || The attacker calls the `Stake` function on the `SMOOFSStaking` contract, transferring their Smoofs NFT and paying the `nftStakeCarryAmount` in MOOVE tokens. || The `Stake` function internally calls `nftCollection.safeTransferFrom(msg.sender, address(this), _tokenId)`, which triggers the `onERC721Received` function in the attacker's contract. || Inside the attacker's `onERC721Received` function, a loop is initiated. This loop repeatedly calls the `SMOOFSStaking.Withdraw(_tokenId, true)` function. || The `Withdraw` function, when `forceWithTax` is true, bypasses the tax logic and allows for repeated reward claims and NFT withdrawals without proper state checks or tax application. || The loop continues until a predefined condition is met (e.g., a certain number of iterations or until the contract's balance is depleted), draining the rewards and potentially the principal from the `SMOOFSStaking` contract. || Finally, the attacker's contract withdraws the NFT and any remaining MOOVE tokens. || The attacker's contract then transfers the drained MOOVE tokens to their own address.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "2 verified, 1 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.95, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploited the `SMOOFSStaking` contract by leveraging the `onERC721Received` function. When the attacker's contract received a Smoofs NFT, the `onERC721Received` function was triggered. Inside this function, a loop repeatedly called the `Withdraw` function with the `forceWithTax` parameter set to `true`. This allowed the attacker to bypass the tax mechanism and repeatedly withdraw rewards associated with the NFT without incurring any penalties, leading to an economic drain of the contract.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `Withdraw` function in `SMOOFSStakingV3` allows for `forceWithTax` to be set to `true`. When this parameter is true, the function does not properly re-check the state or enforce the tax, enabling repeated withdrawals of rewards without the intended tax deduction. This creates an economic exploit where rewards can be drained.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Economic Drain", "attack_title": "Contract : https://polygonscan.com/address/0x367120bf791cc03f040e2574aea0ca7790d3d2e5", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x757c2d1ef0942f7a1b9fc1e618aea3a6f3441a3c", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy", "bytecode_available": false, "chain": {"id": 137, "name": "Polygon"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.20+commit.a1b79de6", "contract_name": "ERC1967Proxy", "explorer_url": "https://polygonscan.com/address/0x757c2d1ef0942f7a1b9fc1e618aea3a6f3441a3c", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0x3b6f71a59aa1ae42eb3ac5bc80b0c4560abe647e", "is_proxy": true, "proxy_type": "EIP1967", "resolution_depth": 1, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:36:36.802Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/access/Ownable.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/interfaces/IERC1967.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/beacon/BeaconProxy.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/beacon/IBeacon.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/beacon/UpgradeableBeacon.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Utils.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/Proxy.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/ProxyAdmin.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol", "data/contracts/2024_02_smoofsstaking/contracts/01_vulnerable_757c2d1e_erc1967proxy/sources/@