{"ai_attack_steps": ["The attacker initiated a flash loan to acquire capital.", "The attacker borrowed DAI from the Compound protocol (cDAI).", "The attacker used the borrowed DAI to mint GoodDollar tokens via the `GDX.buy` function, which is called within the `GoodReserveCDai.buy` function.", "The attacker deployed a malicious staking contract that exploited the reentrancy vulnerability in `GoodFundManager.collectInterest`.", "Within the `collectInterest` function, the attacker's malicious staking contract's `collectUBIInterest` function was called.", "Inside `collectUBIInterest`, the attacker re-entered `GoodFundManager.collectInterest` by calling it again.", "This reentrancy allowed the attacker to repeatedly mint GoodDollar tokens using the same borrowed DAI collateral.", "After minting a large amount of GoodDollar tokens, the attacker sold them for profit.", "Finally, the attacker repaid the initial flash loan and borrowed DAI.", "The attacker drained the system of its assets by exploiting the reentrancy flaw to mint an excessive amount of GoodDollar tokens."], "ai_attack_steps_text": "The attacker initiated a flash loan to acquire capital. || The attacker borrowed DAI from the Compound protocol (cDAI). || The attacker used the borrowed DAI to mint GoodDollar tokens via the `GDX.buy` function, which is called within the `GoodReserveCDai.buy` function. || The attacker deployed a malicious staking contract that exploited the reentrancy vulnerability in `GoodFundManager.collectInterest`. || Within the `collectInterest` function, the attacker's malicious staking contract's `collectUBIInterest` function was called. || Inside `collectUBIInterest`, the attacker re-entered `GoodFundManager.collectInterest` by calling it again. || This reentrancy allowed the attacker to repeatedly mint GoodDollar tokens using the same borrowed DAI collateral. || After minting a large amount of GoodDollar tokens, the attacker sold them for profit. || Finally, the attacker repaid the initial flash loan and borrowed DAI. || The attacker drained the system of its assets by exploiting the reentrancy flaw to mint an excessive amount of GoodDollar tokens.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "2 verified, 1 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.95, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploited a reentrancy vulnerability in the `collectInterest` function of the `GoodFundManager` contract. The `collectInterest` function iterates through a list of staking contracts and calls `collectUBIInterest` on each. The `collectUBIInterest` function in the `MaliciousStakingContract` then calls `GDX.buy` which internally calls `GoodReserveCDai.buy`. The `GoodReserveCDai.buy` function eventually calls `IGoodDollar.mint` which is an ERC20 `mint` function. Crucially, the `GoodFundManager` contract does not implement reentrancy guards. The attacker's malicious staking contract, after being called by `collectInterest`, re-entered the `GoodFundManager` by calling `collectInterest` again within its `collectUBIInterest` callback. This reentrancy allowed the attacker to repeatedly mint GoodDollar tokens using borrowed DAI as collateral before the initial `collectInterest` transaction was completed. The attack involved a flash loan to acquire initial capital, borrowing DAI from cDAI, minting GoodDollar tokens through the GDX exchange, and then repaying the borrowed DAI after draining the system.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "Reentrancy vulnerability in `GoodFundManager.collectInterest` function. The function lacks reentrancy guards, allowing external calls within the function to re-enter `collectInterest` before the initial call's state changes are finalized. Specifically, the `collectUBIInterest` callback from a malicious staking contract can re-enter `collectInterest`, leading to repeated minting of tokens.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy", "attack_title": "Tx : https://app.blocksec.com/explorer/tx/eth/0x726459a46839c915ee2fb3d8de7f986e3c7391c605b7a622112161a84c7384d0", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x0c6c80d2061afa35e160f3799411d83bdeea0a5a", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.8+commit.dddeac2f", "contract_name": "ERC1967Proxy", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x0c6c80d2061afa35e160f3799411d83bdeea0a5a", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0xaacbaab8571cbeceb46ba85b5981efdb8928545e", "is_proxy": true, "proxy_type": "EIP1967", "resolution_depth": 1, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:37:17.505Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy/sources/contracts/utils/ProxyFactory1967.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy/sources/openzeppelin-solidity/contracts/proxy/Proxy.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy/sources/openzeppelin-solidity/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Upgrade.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy/sources/openzeppelin-solidity/contracts/utils/cryptography/ECDSA.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy/sources/openzeppelin-solidity/contracts/proxy/beacon/IBeacon.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy/sources/openzeppelin-solidity/contracts/utils/Address.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/01_vulnerable_0c6c80d2_erc1967proxy/sources/openzeppelin-solidity/contracts/utils/StorageSlot.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The `collectInterest` function in `IGoodFundManager` is vulnerable to reentrancy. The `MaliciousStakingContract` exploits this by calling `GDX.buy` within its `collectUBIInterest` callback, which is triggered by `collectInterest`. This allows the attacker to repeatedly buy GoodDollar tokens using the same borrowed cDAI collateral before the initial transaction is finalized, leading to an inflation of GoodDollar tokens and a drain of DAI.", "verification_status": "proxy"}, {"abi_available": true, "address": "0xaacbaab8571cbeceb46ba85b5981efdb8928545e", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/02_helper_aacbaab8_goodfundmanager", "bytecode_available": false, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.19+commit.7dd6d404", "contract_name": "GoodFundManager", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0xaacbaab8571cbeceb46ba85b5981efdb8928545e", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:37:17.506Z"}, "role": "helper", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/02_helper_aacbaab8_goodfundmanager/sources/@gooddollar/bridge-contracts/contracts/messagePassingBridge/IMessagePassingBridge.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/02_helper_aacbaab8_goodfundmanager/sources/@mean-finance/uniswap-v3-oracle/solidity/interfaces/IStaticOracle.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/02_helper_aacbaab8_goodfundmanager/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/access/AccessControlEnumerableUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/02_helper_aacbaab8_goodfundmanager/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/access/AccessControlUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/02_helper_aacbaab8_goodfundmanager/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/access/IAccessControlEnumerableUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2023_12_gooddollar/contracts/02_helper_aacbaab8_goodfundm