{"ai_attack_steps": ["1. The attacker obtains a flash loan of `iYFI` tokens.", "2. The attacker burns a small amount of `iYFI` tokens, reducing the total supply of `iYFI`.", "3. The attacker deposits a minimal amount of YFI into the `iYFI` lending pool, minting new `iYFI` tokens.", "4. The attacker borrows ETH from the `iETH` pool and WBTC from the `iWBTC` pool.", "5. The attacker calls `withdrawCollateral` for the borrowed ETH and WBTC. Due to a rounding error in the calculation, they receive more collateral than they should have, draining the `iETH` and `iWBTC` pools.", "6. The attacker burns their newly minted `iYFI` tokens. The rounding error in the `withdrawCollateral` function causes them to receive a disproportionately large amount of YFI, draining the `iYFI` pool.", "7. The attacker repays the flash loan.", "8. The attacker profits from the stolen assets."], "ai_attack_steps_text": "1. The attacker obtains a flash loan of `iYFI` tokens. || 2. The attacker burns a small amount of `iYFI` tokens, reducing the total supply of `iYFI`. || 3. The attacker deposits a minimal amount of YFI into the `iYFI` lending pool, minting new `iYFI` tokens. || 4. The attacker borrows ETH from the `iETH` pool and WBTC from the `iWBTC` pool. || 5. The attacker calls `withdrawCollateral` for the borrowed ETH and WBTC. Due to a rounding error in the calculation, they receive more collateral than they should have, draining the `iETH` and `iWBTC` pools. || 6. The attacker burns their newly minted `iYFI` tokens. The rounding error in the `withdrawCollateral` function causes them to receive a disproportionately large amount of YFI, draining the `iYFI` pool. || 7. The attacker repays the flash loan. || 8. The attacker profits from the stolen assets.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "6 verified, 4 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 1.0, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The exploit targets the `withdrawCollateral` function within the bZx protocol. The core vulnerability lies in how the protocol calculates the amount of collateral to be returned to a user. Specifically, it uses integer division which can lead to a rounding down effect. The attacker leverages this by first minting a small amount of `iYFI` tokens. Then, they deposit a tiny amount of YFI into the `iYFI` pool, which mints them `iYFI` tokens. The attacker then borrows ETH and WBTC from the `iETH` and `iWBTC` pools, respectively. The crucial step is when they call `withdrawCollateral`. Due to the rounding down in the calculation of collateral to be returned, the attacker receives more collateral than they are entitled to, effectively draining the pools. This process is repeated for both ETH and WBTC. Finally, the attacker burns their `iYFI` tokens, again exploiting the rounding error to extract a disproportionately large amount of YFI.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The vulnerability stems from a rounding error in the `withdrawCollateral` function of the bZx protocol. When calculating the amount of collateral to return, the protocol uses integer division, which truncates any fractional part. This allows an attacker to withdraw more collateral than they deposited or are entitled to, especially when dealing with small amounts or specific ratios.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Integer Overflow/Underflow", "attack_title": "Tx 2 : https://app.blocksec.com/explorer/tx/eth/0xb072f2e88058c147d8ff643694b43a42e36525b7173ce1daf76e6c06170b0e77", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x7f3fe9d492a9a60aebb06d82cba23c6f32cad10b", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/01_vulnerable_7f3fe9d4_loantoken", "bytecode_available": false, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.5.17+commit.d19bba13", "contract_name": "LoanToken", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x7f3fe9d492a9a60aebb06d82cba23c6f32cad10b", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0xfb772316a54dcd439964b561fc2c173697aeeb5b", "is_proxy": true, "proxy_type": "EIP1967", "resolution_depth": 1, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:37:20.292Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/01_vulnerable_7f3fe9d4_loantoken/source.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The `iYFI.burn` function in the vulnerable contract allows burning of iYFI tokens by any address, including the attacker. The attacker first burns their own iYFI tokens (obtained via a flashloan or other means) to reduce the total supply of iYFI. Then, the attacker deposits a small amount of YFI and mints new iYFI tokens. Due to a rounding issue in the `iYFI.burn` function, when the attacker later burns these newly minted iYFI tokens, they receive a disproportionately large amount of the underlying YFI, effectively draining the pool.", "verification_status": "proxy"}, {"abi_available": false, "address": "0xfb772316a54dcd439964b561fc2c173697aeeb5b", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/02_helper_fb772316_contract", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": null, "contract_name": null, "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0xfb772316a54dcd439964b561fc2c173697aeeb5b", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": false, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:37:20.292Z"}, "role": "helper", "source_available": false, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/02_helper_fb772316_contract/bytecode.txt", "data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/02_helper_fb772316_contract/NO_SOURCE.txt"], "source_hint": "implementation of 0x7f3fe9d492a9a60aebb06d82cba23c6f32cad10b", "verification_status": "unverified"}, {"abi_available": true, "address": "0xb983e01458529665007ff7e0cddecdb74b967eb6", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/03_vulnerable_b983e014_loantoken", "bytecode_available": false, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.5.17+commit.d19bba13", "contract_name": "LoanToken", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0xb983e01458529665007ff7e0cddecdb74b967eb6", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0x9e1341a201b1aecb1b0dd584989790a0232b4af5", "is_proxy": true, "proxy_type": "EIP1967", "resolution_depth": 1, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:37:20.292Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/03_vulnerable_b983e014_loantoken/source.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The `iETH.borrow` function is used to borrow ETH. The vulnerability lies in how collateral is handled. After borrowing, the attacker calls `withdrawCollateral` which, due to a rounding issue, allows them to withdraw more collateral than they should have, effectively draining the ETH pool.", "verification_status": "proxy"}, {"abi_available": true, "address": "0x9e1341a201b1aecb1b0dd584989790a0232b4af5", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/04_helper_9e1341a2_loantokenlogicweth", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.5.17+commit.d19bba13", "contract_name": "LoanTokenLogicWeth", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x9e1341a201b1aecb1b0dd584989790a0232b4af5", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:37:20.293Z"}, "role": "helper", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_12_bzx/contracts/04_helper_9e1341a2_loantokenlogicweth/source.sol"], "source_hint": "implementation of 0xb983e01458529665007ff7e0cddecdb74b967eb6", "verification_status": "verified"}, {"abi_available": true, "a