e attacker gained control of two private keys belonging to owners of the multisig wallet. By using these two compromised keys, the attacker was able to submit a transaction to transfer USDT from the multisig wallet to their own address. The `submitTransaction` function in the `MultiSigWallet` contract first adds the transaction and then automatically calls `confirmTransaction` for the submitter. Subsequently, the attacker used the second compromised private key to call `confirmTransaction` again for the same transaction. Since the `confirmTransaction` function also calls `executeTransaction` if the transaction becomes confirmed (i.e., reaches the `required` number of confirmations), the transaction was executed, transferring the USDT to the attacker's address. The exploit was successful because the multisig contract did not have sufficient safeguards against compromised owner keys or a mechanism to detect malicious activity when multiple confirmations come from addresses associated with compromised keys.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "Compromised Private Keys / Access Control", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Access Control", "attack_title": "Harmony_multisig_exp", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x715cdda5e9ad30a0ced14940f9997ee611496de6", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2022_06_harmony_multisig/contracts/01_vulnerable_715cdda5_multisigwallet", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.5.17+commit.d19bba13", "contract_name": "MultiSigWallet", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x715cdda5e9ad30a0ced14940f9997ee611496de6", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:39:38.357Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2022_06_harmony_multisig/contracts/01_vulnerable_715cdda5_multisigwallet/so