` function on the legitimate `XToken` contract, providing the same `orderId` but with a zero `borrowAmount`. This allowed the attacker to drain the ETH collateral from the `XToken` contract without any prior debt or liquidation. || The attacker repeated this process multiple times using different payload contracts to maximize the stolen funds.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "1 verified, 0 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.75, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploited a vulnerability in XCarnival's `XNFT.sol` contract. The `pledgeAndBorrow` function, when called with a malicious `xToken` (a contract that does nothing, `INothing`), allowed the attacker to pledge an NFT and borrow assets without creating a real debt. The NFT was effectively locked, but no loan was issued. The attacker then used `withdrawNFT` to retrieve the NFT and subsequently drained ETH from the `XToken` contract by calling its `borrow` function with a valid `orderId` but a zero-value debt.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `pledgeAndBorrow` function in `XNFT.sol` did not properly validate the `xToken` address. This allowed the attacker to supply a malicious `xToken` contract that did not perform any actual lending operations, leading to the NFT being locked without a corresponding debt. The `withdrawNFT` function could then be used to retrieve the NFT, and the `XToken.borrow` function could be used to drain funds.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Logic Error", "attack_title": "er was call `pledgeAndBorrow()`, But `pledge()` also vulnerable.", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x39360ac1239a0b98cb8076d4135d0f72b7fd9909", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.2+commit.661d1103", "contract_name": "XNFT", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x39360ac1239a0b98cb8076d4135d0f72b7fd9909", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:39:43.170Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/XNFT.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/interface/IP2Controller.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/interface/IXToken.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/library/SafeERC20.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/interface/IXAirDrop.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/interface/IPunks.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/interface/IWrappedPunks.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/token/ERC721/IERC721Upgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/token/ERC721/IERC721ReceiverUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/token/ERC1155/IERC1155Upgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/token/ERC1155/IERC1155ReceiverUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/utils/math/SafeMathUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/proxy/utils/Initializable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/interface/IERC20.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/interface/IInterestRateModel.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/library/SafeMath.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/contracts/library/Address.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/token/ERC721/extensions/IERC721EnumerableUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/utils/introspection/IERC165Upgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival/contracts/01_vulnerable_39360ac1_xnft/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/utils/AddressUpgradeable.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The `pledgeAndBorrow` function in `XNFT.sol` allows users to pledge an NFT and borrow assets. The vulnerability lies in the fact that the `pledge` function, which is called internally by `pledgeAndBorrow`, does not properly validate the `xToken` address. This allows an attacker to provide a malicious `xToken` contract (in this case, `INothing`) that does not actually perform any lending or borrowing operations. When `pledgeAndBorrow` is called with this malicious `xToken`, the NFT is effectively locked in the `XNFT` contract without any corresponding debt being created. The attacker can then withdraw the NFT using `withdrawNFT` and subsequently drain any available ETH from the `XToken` contract using the `borrow` function, as the `orderId` is incremented and used to track the pledged NFT.", "verification_status": "verified"}], "contracts_dir": "data/contracts/2022_06_xcarnival", "id": "2022_06_xcarnival", "metadata": {