{"ai_attack_steps": ["The attacker identified a valid transaction on the Nomad Bridge, which involved a user sending assets (e.g., WBTC).", "The attacker copied the calldata of this legitimate transaction.", "The attacker modified the recipient address within the copied calldata to their own address.", "The attacker submitted this modified calldata to the Nomad Bridge's `Replica.process` function.", "Because the `process` function did not adequately check if the message had already been processed, it executed the transaction again, sending the specified amount of assets to the attacker's address.", "The attacker repeated this process to drain a significant amount of funds from the bridge."], "ai_attack_steps_text": "The attacker identified a valid transaction on the Nomad Bridge, which involved a user sending assets (e.g., WBTC). || The attacker copied the calldata of this legitimate transaction. || The attacker modified the recipient address within the copied calldata to their own address. || The attacker submitted this modified calldata to the Nomad Bridge's `Replica.process` function. || Because the `process` function did not adequately check if the message had already been processed, it executed the transaction again, sending the specified amount of assets to the attacker's address. || The attacker repeated this process to drain a significant amount of funds from the bridge.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "2 verified, 1 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.95, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The Nomad Bridge allowed users to deposit assets on one chain and withdraw them on another. The core of the bridge's cross-chain communication was handled by a system of 'replicas' on each chain, which processed messages from other domains. The vulnerability lay in the `Replica.process` function. This function was responsible for verifying messages and dispatching them to their intended recipients. Crucially, it relied on a `confirmAt` mapping to check if a message's root had been sufficiently confirmed. However, the `process` function did not adequately check if the message being processed had already been marked as `LEGACY_STATUS_PROCESSED`. An attacker could exploit this by sending a valid message, then immediately calling `process` with the same message data but with a modified recipient address. Because the `process` function didn't check if the message was already processed, it would re-process the message, sending funds to the attacker's address. The attacker essentially replayed a legitimate transaction, but directed the funds to themselves. The provided transaction `0xa5fe9d044e4f3e5aa5bc4c0709333cd2190cba0f4e7f16bcf73f49f83e4a5460` shows a user sending 0.01 WBTC, and the attacker then used a similar calldata structure to process a message for 100 WBTC to their own address.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `Replica.process` function failed to properly check if a message had already been processed (`LEGACY_STATUS_PROCESSED`). This allowed an attacker to replay a valid message by modifying the recipient address, effectively tricking the bridge into sending funds to the attacker's address.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy", "attack_title": "er send 0.01 WBTC to NomadBridge : 0xed26708a7335116bdb0673f32ace7c2f329fe3cd349e200447210f1721f335f0", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x5d94309e5a0090b165fa4181519701637b6daeba", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/01_vulnerable_5d94309e_upgradebeaconproxy", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.7.6+commit.7338295f", "contract_name": "UpgradeBeaconProxy", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x5d94309e5a0090b165fa4181519701637b6daeba", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": "0x7f221a1850c12b57fed1f0831dd25399a13b68c2", "is_proxy": true, "proxy_type": "EIP1967", "resolution_depth": 1, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:39:47.478Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/01_vulnerable_5d94309e_upgradebeaconproxy/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/upgrade/UpgradeBeaconProxy.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/01_vulnerable_5d94309e_upgradebeaconproxy/sources/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/utils/Address.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The Nomad Replica contract's `process` function was vulnerable to a replay attack. Attackers could copy valid transaction data from one chain and replay it on another, or replay transactions with a modified recipient address. This was due to insufficient validation of the message's origin and the lack of proper checks on the Merkle root and leaf nodes, allowing the attacker to submit a malicious update that was accepted as valid.", "verification_status": "proxy"}, {"abi_available": true, "address": "0x7f221a1850c12b57fed1f0831dd25399a13b68c2", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica", "bytecode_available": false, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.7.6+commit.7338295f", "contract_name": "Replica", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0x7f221a1850c12b57fed1f0831dd25399a13b68c2", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:39:47.478Z"}, "role": "helper", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts/cryptography/ECDSA.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/access/OwnableUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/proxy/Initializable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/utils/AddressUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/node_modules/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/utils/ContextUpgradeable.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/node_modules/@summa-tx/memview-sol/contracts/SafeMath.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/node_modules/@summa-tx/memview-sol/contracts/TypedMemView.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/NomadBase.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/Replica.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/Version0.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/interfaces/IMessageRecipient.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/libs/Merkle.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/libs/Message.sol", "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge/contracts/02_helper_7f221a18_replica/sources/packages/contracts-core/contracts/libs/TypeCasts.sol"], "source_hint": "implementation of 0x5d94309e5a0090b165fa4181519701637b6daeba", "verification_status": "verified"}], "contracts_dir": "data/contracts/2022_08_nomadbridge", "id": "2022_08_nomadbridge", "metadata": {"ai_enabled": true, "ai_model": "gemini-2.5-flash-lite|gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "dataset_