{"ai_attack_steps": ["The attacker initiated a flash loan from Aave.", "During the flash loan callback (`executeOperation`), the attacker called the `LibertiVault.deposit` function.", "Inside the `deposit` function, the attacker used the `data` parameter to call the `oneInchV4Router.swap` function, which in turn called the `LibertiVault.deposit` function again (reentrancy).", "In the second `deposit` call, the attacker manipulated the `data` parameter to ensure that the `swap` function returned a larger amount of `USDT` than expected, effectively minting more shares than they should have based on their initial deposit.", "After the reentrant calls, the attacker exited the vault using `LibertiVault.exit()`, withdrawing a disproportionately large amount of assets due to the inflated share count.", "The attacker repaid the flash loan.", "The attacker transferred the stolen funds to their own address.", "The attacker converted the stolen `USDT` to `WETH` using a Uniswap V3 router."], "ai_attack_steps_text": "The attacker initiated a flash loan from Aave. || During the flash loan callback (`executeOperation`), the attacker called the `LibertiVault.deposit` function. || Inside the `deposit` function, the attacker used the `data` parameter to call the `oneInchV4Router.swap` function, which in turn called the `LibertiVault.deposit` function again (reentrancy). || In the second `deposit` call, the attacker manipulated the `data` parameter to ensure that the `swap` function returned a larger amount of `USDT` than expected, effectively minting more shares than they should have based on their initial deposit. || After the reentrant calls, the attacker exited the vault using `LibertiVault.exit()`, withdrawing a disproportionately large amount of assets due to the inflated share count. || The attacker repaid the flash loan. || The attacker transferred the stolen funds to their own address. || The attacker converted the stolen `USDT` to `WETH` using a Uniswap V3 router.", "ai_confidence_has_source_code": true, "ai_confidence_known_pattern_match": true, "ai_confidence_reasoning": "1 verified, 0 proxy", "ai_confidence_score": 0.75, "ai_confidence_verified_contracts": true, "ai_explanation": "The attacker exploited a reentrancy vulnerability in the `LibertiVault.deposit` function. During a flash loan callback, the attacker re-entered the `deposit` function. This reentrancy allowed them to manipulate the share calculation, effectively minting more shares than their deposited assets warranted. Subsequently, they exited the vault with a disproportionately large amount of assets.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `LibertiVault.deposit` function lacks proper reentrancy guards. The function allows external calls (implicitly through the `data` parameter which can trigger other contract interactions) before updating the internal state related to share calculation, enabling the reentrant call to manipulate the share minting logic.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy", "attack_title": "Tx : https://polygonscan.com/tx/0x7320accea0ef1d7abca8100c82223533b624c82d3e8d445954731495d4388483", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0x9c80a455ecaca7025a45f5fa3b85fd6a462a447b", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2023_07_libertify/contracts/01_vulnerable_9c80a455_libertivault", "bytecode_available": true, "chain": {"id": 137, "name": "Polygon"}, "compiler_version": "v0.8.17+commit.8df45f5f", "contract_name": "LibertiVault", "explorer_url": "https://polygonscan.com/address/0x9c80a455ecaca7025a45f5fa3b85fd6a462a447b", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:42:20.148Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2023_07_libertify/contracts/01_vulnerable_9c80a455_libertivault/sources/@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/access/OwnableUpgradeable.sol", "d