ely gave the attacker full control over the wallet. Once the attacker became an owner with zero required confirmations, they could then use the `execute` function to transfer all the Ether from the wallet to their own address.", "ai_mitigation": [], "ai_root_cause": "The `initWallet` function in the Parity Wallet contract lacked a check to ensure it was only called once. This allowed an attacker to re-initialize the wallet, add themselves as an owner with zero required confirmations, and subsequently drain the funds.", "ai_vulnerability_type": "Reentrancy", "attack_title": "Tx : https://etherscan.io/tx/0xeef10fc5170f669b86c4cd0444882a96087221325f8bf2f55d6188633aa7be7c", "contracts": [{"abi_available": true, "address": "0xbec591de75b8699a3ba52f073428822d0bfc0d7e", "artifact_dir": "data/contracts/2017_07_parity_first_hack/contracts/01_vulnerable_bec591de_wallet", "bytecode_available": false, "chain": {"id": 1, "name": "Ethereum"}, "compiler_version": "v0.4.9+commit.364da425", "contract_name": "Wallet", "explorer_url": "https://etherscan.io/address/0xbec591de75b8699a3ba52f073428822d0bfc0d7e", "fetch_error": null, "is_verified": true, "proxy": {"admin_address": null, "implementation_address": null, "is_proxy": false, "proxy_type": null, "resolution_depth": 0, "resolved_at": "2026-04-10T06:42:29.640Z"}, "role": "vulnerable", "source_available": true, "source_files": ["data/contracts/2017_07_parity_first_hack/contracts/01_vulnerable_bec591de_wallet/source.sol"], "source_hint": "AI extracted: The `initWallet` function in the Parity Wallet contract could be called multiple times, allowing an attacker to become an owner and drain the contract's funds.", "verification_status": "verified"}], "contracts_dir": "data/contracts/2017_07_parity_first_hack", "id": "2017_07_parity_first_hack", "metadata": {"ai_enabled": true, "ai_model": "gemini-2.5-flash-lite|gemini-2.5-flash-lite", "dataset_version": "1.0.0", "poc_parser_version": "1.0.0", "processed_at": "2026-04-10T06:42:31.231Z"}